# Tab while pinyin is typed belongs to the input method: rime-ice's key_binder sends it on as Shift+Right (the cursor
# to the next syllable; rime-ice's default.yaml, fetched into ThirdParty/rime-data: "Tab / Shift+Tab 切换光标至下/上一个拼音"), and the Rime
# wrapper lists Tab among the keys that edit the composition and never commit it (RimeSession.editingKeys). Nothing goes
# in, the focus stays, the pinyin stays marked and its candidates stay up. (Tab inserting a row is the other panels':
# the command list, suggestions, clipboard history, the user guide's "Every panel works the same way".) Seen on a real
# Mac 2026-11-15: the marked text stayed "nihao".
# QUESTION: the format can't check where the cursor inside the marked text is (after "ni"), only the marked string.
NAME Tab during pinyin stays with the input method: nothing goes in and the pinyin stays marked
PROFILES all
LANG chinese
TEXT "Hi |"
TYPE nihao
EXPECT panel shown
KEY tab
EXPECT doc "Hi "
EXPECT marked "nihao"
EXPECT panel shown
